Customer Data Visualization using PCA
Problem Statement
           Modern businesses collect customer information from multiple sources. Customer datasets may contain several numerical features, making direct visualization and analysis difficult. Therefore, a dimensionality reduction technique is required to simplify the data while retaining important information. This project uses Principal Component Analysis to reduce customer data into principal components and visualize customer patterns. K-Means clustering can further be used to identify customer segments.
Objective
        To analyze and visualize customer data using Principal Component Analysis (PCA) by reducing multiple customer attributes into a smaller number of principal components while preserving maximum variance.
