PCA Methodology
 What is PCA?
          Principal Component Analysis is a dimensionality reduction technique used to transform a dataset containing multiple correlated variables into a smaller set of uncorrelated principal components.
 Why PCA?
 Many features
     ↓
Difficult to visualize
     ↓
  PCA
     ↓
Fewer dimensions
     ↓
Easy visualization
